\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The four generation protocols behind the estimands. Fill encodes the cache condition while a span is processed (grey $=$ full cache; hatched $=$ compression active); the text in each span says where its tokens come from (self-generated versus teacher-forced replay of exact stored token IDs). Forward readout scores answer generation \emph  {under compression} given the full-cache reference trace; reverse readout scores \emph  {full-cache} answer generation given the compressed model's own trace. The residual $\rho (m) = \Delta _{\mathrm  {tot}}(m) - \Delta _{\mathrm  {ro}}(m)$ is the free-running loss unexplained by on-reference readout; the forward and reverse estimates bracket the on-policy residual (\cref  {sec:reverse}).}}{7}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:protocol}{{1}{7}{The four generation protocols behind the estimands. Fill encodes the cache condition while a span is processed (grey $=$ full cache; hatched $=$ compression active); the text in each span says where its tokens come from (self-generated versus teacher-forced replay of exact stored token IDs). Forward readout scores answer generation \emph {under compression} given the full-cache reference trace; reverse readout scores \emph {full-cache} answer generation given the compressed model's own trace. The residual $\res {m} = \dtot {m} - \dro {m}$ is the free-running loss unexplained by on-reference readout; the forward and reverse estimates bracket the on-policy residual (\cref {sec:reverse})}{figure.caption.5}{}}
\newlabel{fig:protocol@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][6][]7}{}{}{}}
